{#
  The Gallery, LaTeX family. One Race's Image Assets, art and names only — a
  printable art sheet, with the rules left to the Race Overview.

  The Markdown twin at `markdown/gallery/main.md.jinja` shows the same entries
  in the same order. Only this one carries no cross-links: a printed sheet
  cannot be clicked, so every caption is plain text (ADR 0005 — each family
  spells the same view-model its own way).

  `\includegraphics` takes the committed Asset's own absolute path, so this
  Product embeds the full-size original the way the Army Reference does. The
  Markdown family's `image_src` filter is not applied here.
-#}
\documentclass[a4paper,12pt]{article}
\usepackage[margin=2cm]{geometry}
\usepackage{textcomp}
\usepackage{graphicx}
\usepackage{fancyhdr}

% A tiny version stamp in the footer of every page. `\maketitle` switches its
% own page to the `plain` style, so `plain` is redefined to match.
\newcommand{\versionfoot}{%
  \fancyhf{}%
  \fancyfoot[C]{\thepage}%
  \fancyfoot[R]{\tiny v\VAR{spf_version}}%
  \renewcommand{\headrulewidth}{0pt}%
}
\pagestyle{fancy}
\versionfoot
\fancypagestyle{plain}{\versionfoot}

\title{\VAR{source.title | latex_escape} --- Gallery}
\author{}
\date{}

\begin{document}
\maketitle
\BLOCK{for entry in source.entries}

\begin{center}
\includegraphics[width=0.7\textwidth,height=0.7\textheight,keepaspectratio]{\VAR{entry.image | posix_path}}

\textbf{\VAR{entry.name | latex_escape}}
\end{center}
\BLOCK{endfor}
\end{document}
